    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full build passes green. Here's a summary of what I implemented for the soft-delete change.\n\n## Changes\n\n**1. `Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a `deleted` field (`@Column(name = \"deleted\", nullable = false)`, defaulting to `false`) with `isDeleted()`/`setDeleted(...)` accessors. A newly built owner keeps the default `false`.\n\n**2. `DeleteOwner` function** (`rest/function/owner/DeleteOwner.java`) \u2014 now flags the owner deleted and saves it instead of removing the row:\n```java\nowner.setDeleted(true);\nownerRepository.save(owner);\n```\nThe DELETE pipeline (`LoadOwner \u2192 DeleteOwner \u2192 RespondWithNoContent`) still returns 204 (2xx), and since the row is retained, a later GET returns the owner with `deleted: true`.\n\n**3. Create-endpoint checks now ignore deleted owners** \u2014 added an early `if (existing.isDeleted()) continue;` guard to the two steps the spec names:\n- `EnsureUniqueIdentity` \u2014 the household duplicate block (409)\n- `FlagPossibleDuplicate` \u2014 the possible-duplicate flagging\n\nSo a normally-blocking duplicate is allowed when the only matching owner has been soft-deleted.\n\n**4. OpenAPI schema** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 added a read-only `deleted` boolean to the `Owner` schema, which regenerates `OwnerDto` with the field; MapStruct auto-maps `Owner.deleted \u2192 OwnerDto.deleted`, so GET responses expose it.\n\n**5. DB schemas** \u2014 added `deleted BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE NOT NULL` to the `owners` table in all four dialects (hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql). The test profile uses hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema column is required; HSQLDB needs `DEFAULT` before `NOT NULL`, which is what tripped the first run.\n\n## Tests\n`./mvnw -o test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, all tests green, including the new `AcceptanceTest` cases `coreSoftDeleteFlagsAndRetains` and `coreDeletedOwnerIgnoredByDuplicateCheck`.",
